--TEST--
`Class::method(...)` and `self::method(...)` are `E0136` with a fix that drops the `(...)`, and `$obj->method(...)` keeps its form — `rule:expressions/method-reference`
--FILE--
<?nvs
final class Prices {
    public static function double(int $n): int {
        return $n * 2;
    }

    public function less(int $n): int {
        return $n - 1;
    }

    public static function viaSelf(): callable {
        return self::double(...);
    }
}

callable $double = Prices::double(...);
// On an object the `(...)` stays, because `$prices->less` would read a property.
Prices $prices = new Prices();
callable $less = $prices->less(...);
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0136]: a method reference on a class is written without `(...)`
   --> %s:12:28
   |
12 |         return self::double(...);
   |                            ^^^^^ delete this
   = suggestion: write the reference without `(...)` (delete)

error[E0136]: a method reference on a class is written without `(...)`
   --> %s:16:34
   |
16 | callable $double = Prices::double(...);
   |                                  ^^^^^ delete this
   = suggestion: write the reference without `(...)` (delete)

error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
